<title>UK: Ghana weekly cocoa purchases ahead of last year.</title>
<headline>Ghana weekly cocoa purchases ahead of last year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ghana cocoa purchases in the 17th week of the 1996/97 season ending February 6 were 8,687 tonnes compared with 6,229 tonnes in the week ending February 8 of the last season.</p>
<p>The Ghana Cocoa Board said cumulative purchases to the end of the 17th week had totalled 281,558 tonnes. This compares with 318,371 tonnes in the corresponding year-ago period.</p>
<p>The latest figure points to a drop from the 16th week when 12,365 tonnes were purchased.</p>
<p>In the 17th week of the 1995/96 season ending on February 1 the Board had purchased 8,275 tonnes of cocoa with the cumulative reaching 312,142 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom +44-171-542 8072</p>
</text>
